  map.set('contracts/openapi.json', '{\n  "openapi": "3.1.0",\n  "info": {\n    "title": "Couli rebate-platform API",\n    "version": "0.9.0",\n    "summary": "Shared HTTP contract for the app, H5, admin console and backend.",\n    "description": "Single source for endpoints (D17); error codes and enums live in contracts/error-codes.yaml and\\ncontracts/enums/*.yaml. Conventions: 规划/04 §5; authoring rules: contracts/README.md.\\nv0.9 (CT-02a) covers the path 登录 → 搜索 → 转链跳转; the rest is added per feature.\\n\\nEvery business response uses the envelope `{code, msg, data, trace_id}`; `code=0` is success.\\nOperation extensions: `x-auth` (none | optional | login | phone | realname, 04 §5),\\n`x-signed` (true = X-Timestamp / X-Nonce / X-Sign required, BR-ID-09),\\n`x-idempotent` (true = Idempotency-Key required, 04 §6 mark I),\\n`x-error-codes` (business codes the operation may return besides the common ones;\\nmeaning, client action and data shape per code in contracts/error-codes.yaml),\\n`x-implementation: planned` (declared ahead of its route, TECH-05; removed when the route\\nships, apps/api/src/contract.test.ts enforces both ways),\\n`x-step-up` (the step_up_action the `X-Step-Up-Token` header must carry, 04 §5; only the four\\noperations of the 04 §5 step-up row: POST /v1/withdrawals → withdraw, PUT\\n/v1/me/payout-account → payout_account_change, POST /v1/me/phone → phone_change,\\nPOST /v1/me/deletion → account_deletion. Such an operation is idempotent, lists the\\nX-Step-Up-Token parameter and the codes 10003 (token missing, expired or for another action)\\nand 20903 (its Idempotency-Key was abandoned through POST /v1/idempotency-keys/abandon).\\nWhen only some requests need step-up, the condition is written in the operation\\ndescription: POST /v1/me/phone needs it only for a change, not for a first binding).\\n`x-min-version-gate` (true | false | conditional, 04 §5 最低支持版本): on every /v1 write\\noperation (not on GET); true = a client of the three apps below the minimum supported\\nversion gets 10405; false and conditional only for the operations the interface table of\\nBR-ID-01 细则「最低支持版本的接口层拦截」 lists, the condition written in the description.\\n`x-session-scopes` (array of session_scope, 04 §5 受限会话): [full, deletion_only] on the\\noperations of the table in BR-ID-01 细则「受限会话」 (with the condition in the description\\nwhere only some request bodies are accepted); not marked = [full].\\nCommon codes any operation may return: 10401, 10402, 10403, 20001, 42901, 44001, 44002,\\n50001, 50401; with x-auth login also 10001, 10002, 10006; with Idempotency-Key also 20901,\\n40901. Any operation called with a bearer token may also return 10405 when it does not accept\\nthe token\'s session scope (x-session-scopes); operations whose version gate is true or\\nconditional, and the restricted logins, list 10405 in x-error-codes.\\n\\nAdmin console operations live under /admin/v1 (04 §6.6; CT-02f adds auth, me/permissions and\\nthe read-only admins list). Their `x-auth` takes enum admin_auth_level: none (the login\\nsteps; the intermediate `login_ticket` goes in the request body), admin (admin_token) or\\nsuper (admin_token of a super admin). After login every request carries\\n`Authorization: Bearer <admin_token>` (security scheme adminBearerAuth); the token is never a\\ncookie, so there is no CSRF token. Admin step-up tokens go in the `X-Step-Up-Token` header.\\nThey are not app requests: no X-App-Id / X-Platform / X-Device-Id, no request signature, no\\nversion gate, no session scopes; lists page with `page` and `page_size` ≤ 200. Common codes\\nof every admin operation: 10403 (data.reason=admin_ip_not_allowed), 20001, 42901, 50001;\\nwith admin or super also 10001 and 10403 (data.reason=admin_permission_denied). An operation\\nguarded by a permission point (enum admin_permission) names it in its description\\n(「Permission point `<key>`」); console writes use CAS where state is replaced (20902 with\\ndata.resource) and, except the original-route refunds, the recon-diff close, write-off and\\nrestore, the supplement batch launch and the union receipt entry and reversal, carry no\\nIdempotency-Key (04 §6.6).\\n"\n  },\n  "servers": [\n    {\n      "url": "http://127.0.0.1:3100",\n      "description": "Local `api` entry (API_HOST / API_PORT defaults)."\n    }\n  ],\n  "tags": [\n    {\n      "name": "ops",\n      "description": "Operational probes. Not part of the product API and not versioned under /v1."\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "identity",\n      "description": "Device registration, SMS login, token refresh and the current user (04 §6.1)."\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "growth",\n      "description": "Invite binding and relations (growth module)."\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "config",\n      "description": "Client configuration and switches (04 §6.2, §10.1)."\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "trade",\n      "description": "Search, product detail, input parsing, link open / convert, the link landing page and the share page (04 §6.3)."\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "union",\n      "description": "Union authorization and binding (04 §6.3)."\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "order",\n      "description": "Orders and pending-track cards (04 §6.4)."\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "fund",\n      "description": "Payout account, withdrawals, wallet and the earnings dashboard (04 §6.1, §6.4)."\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "pay",\n      "description": "Pay orders of the native apps — create with the channel launch parameters, status, return from the SDK and cancel (WeChat Pay APP and Alipay App payment; not callable from H5, JSBridge or the Agent; 04 §6.4, BR-PAY-01～05)."\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "content",\n      "description": "Articles, notices, update check, inbox messages and page preview (04 §6.2, §6.4)."\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "admin-auth",\n      "description": "Admin console login (password, first password change, authenticator binding and code), step-up in two tiers and the signed-in account\'s permission points (04 §6.6 auth, BR-ID-34)."\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "admin-accounts",\n      "description": "Admin accounts and their management — create, disable and enable, permission points, authenticator reset, display name and verify phone; super admin only (04 §6.6 admins, §11)."\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "admin-audit",\n      "description": "Admin audit log search and record detail; own records only without permission point audit.view_all (04 §6.6 audit-logs, §11.1; F-ADM-03)."\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "admin-exports",\n      "description": "Admin export tasks — create from a list\'s filters (asynchronous CSV, masked by default), list (own tasks, or everyone\'s with audit.view_all), creator-only short-lived download link and retry of a failed task (permission point export; 01 F-ADM-03, 04 §6.6 exports, §11.1, BR-ID-34)."\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "admin-users",\n      "description": "App users in the admin console — list, lookup, detail, direct invitees, audited reveal, level and inviter changes, ban / freeze and union binding reset / disable / enable (permission points user.*, pii.*, risk.*, union.binding_*; 04 §6.6, §11; F1-07)."\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "admin-search",\n      "description": "Admin console top-bar search — one box for an order number, withdrawal number, full phone number or UID, trimmed to the account\'s permission points (order.view, user.lookup, fund.view; 01 F-ADM-04, 04 §6.6 search, BR-ID-34)."\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "admin-orders",\n      "description": "Admin order console — the sub-order list with filters and one sub-order with its status history, commission snapshot and link records (permission point order.view, or user.lookup together with user_id; 01 F-ADM-05, 04 §6.6 orders, §11); the writes of CT-24n are manual sync and its records (order.view), Excel import of rights / punish / channel orders (order.claim), hold / unhold (order.hold) and assigning an unattributed order (order.assign)."\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "admin-claims",\n      "description": "Admin order claim review — the list with filters and per-status counts and one claim with its child orders and evidence view, read only (permission point order.claim, or user.lookup together with user_id; 01 F-ADM-06, 04 §6.6 claims, §11, BR-ATTR-18). Approve and reject follow in CT-24l."\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "admin-content",\n      "description": "Admin content operations; platform mark replacement images (permission point content.platform_icon, BR-TEXT-24)."\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "admin-notify",\n      "description": "Admin notification channels — per template code the push / SMS switches with SMS readiness, and the SMS signature and template CODE registration saved as pending with a synchronous test send to the operator\'s verify phone, retest, enable and discard (permission points content.article or notify.channels to read, notify.channels to write, fund codes also content.fund_terms to save or enable; 04 §3, §11.2; BR-TEXT-20, BR-TEXT-09)."\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "admin-config",\n      "description": "Admin configuration center and emergency switches (permission points config.* and switch.*, 04 §10, §10.2, §11.2; F1-10)."\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "admin-risk",\n      "description": "Admin risk rule list — every rule with its status and threshold configuration keys, and enable / disable (permission point config.risk, step-up for the writes; thresholds stay under /admin/v1/config-items; 04 §6.6 risk-rules, §11.2, BR-ID-36)."\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "admin-appeals",\n      "description": "Admin risk appeal console — the appeal list with filters and four counts, one appeal with its risk hit records and blocked request, claim (a mark, not exclusive), resolve (upheld / revoked; revoking a ban, a freeze or a blocklist block also needs risk.ban, risk.freeze or risk.blocklist with a totp step-up), registering an appeal on a person\'s behalf, and the lookup of requests blocked with 44001 (permission point risk.appeal; 04 §6.6 appeals, §11.2, BR-ID-36, BR-ID-31)."\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "admin-dashboard",\n      "description": "Admin console workbench — to-do counts, yesterday\'s overview and system status, trimmed to the account\'s permission points (permission point dashboard.view, 01 F-ADM-26, 04 §6.6 dashboard, §11.1)."\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "admin-unions",\n      "description": "Station-owner union accounts and PIDs (推广位) in the admin console — accounts with authorization expiry and probe results, OAuth re-authorization sessions and their completion, manual credential entry, alert phones, and PID registration, change of pending rows, activation with the 花卷云 ignore confirmation and retirement (permission points union.account_auth, union.pid; 04 §6.6 union-accounts, union-pids, §11.2; BR-ID-24, BR-ATTR-02)."\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "admin-pay",\n      "description": "Admin pay console — pay orders with their refunds and channel request summaries, the manual settlement of a needs_manual pay order (step-up), original-route refunds of a pay order or a pay anomaly (Idempotency-Key, no step-up), the refund list, pay anomalies and the R4 reconciliation differences (permission points pay.view, pay.resolve, pay.refund; 04 §6.6 pay-orders, §11.2; BR-PAY-05, BR-PAY-06, BR-PAY-07)."\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "admin-recon",\n      "description": "Admin reconciliation console — the R1–R3 reconciliation differences (差错单) page by page with filters and one difference with its handling summary, read only (permission point fund.recon or fund.view; 01 F-ADM-08, 04 §3.2 recon_diffs, §11). Handling a difference follows in CT-24w; source R4 stays under admin-pay."\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "admin-adjustments",\n      "description": "Admin adjustments and bad-debt write-offs — manual adjustment forms page by page and one form with its balance preview, read with permission point fund.adjust or fund.view; submitting an adjustment or a whole-form reversal in one step, approving a system-prefilled ACCOUNT_CLOSED form (sms step-up) and rejecting it (no step-up); write-off candidates, read with fund.writeoff or fund.view, and approving one with fund.writeoff (sms step-up; 01 F-ADM-08, 04 §3.2 admin_adjustments, bad_debt_writeoffs, §11; BR-FUND-24, BR-FUND-12)."\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "admin-withdrawals",\n      "description": "Admin withdrawal console — the withdrawal list with filters and one withdrawal with its amounts, batch, transfer attempt summaries, holds in effect, automatic payout decision and risk flags, read only, payee data masked (permission point withdraw.review or fund.view; 01 F-ADM-07, 04 §3.2 withdrawals, §11). Review, rejection, batch and manual payouts, automatic payout settings and cancelling a WeChat transfer follow in later tasks."\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "admin-settle-bills",\n      "description": "Admin monthly settlement console — the monthly settlement bills with their derived status, bill-day totals (display only) and batch summaries, and the items of one batch, read with permission point settle.bill or fund.view, and the batch writes with settle.bill and a totp step-up (confirm now or at a set time, cancel a schedule, reject, continue, launch supplement batches; 01 F-ADM-08, 04 §3.2 settle_bills, settle_batches, settle_batch_items, §11; BR-FUND-04). The manual start (SB10), the statement upload and a supplement pre-check follow in later tasks."\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "admin-asset-snapshots",\n      "description": "Admin asset snapshots — the daily asset snapshots (one row per accounting day, with the per-platform union receivables) page by page, read only (permission point fund.view; 01 F-ADM-08, 04 §3.2 asset_snapshots, asset_snapshot_receivables, §11; BR-FUND-18). The daily ledger with W / P and the water-level state, the union collection entry (fund.cash_entry), the fund dashboard and the export follow in later tasks."\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "admin-fund-ledger",\n      "description": "Admin platform fund ledger — the union collection entry and its whole-record reversal (permission point fund.cash_entry, totp step-up), the list of union collection records and the fund ledger overview, the last two read only (permission point fund.view; 01 F-ADM-08, 04 §3.2 union_receipts, §11; BR-FUND-20, BR-WDR-18). The entry of the enterprise Alipay balance W belongs to the payout console (design/specs/admin-payouts.md)."\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "agent",\n      "description": "Agent sessions, history, the reply stream, stop, feedback and report (04 §6.5, §8)."\n    }\n  ],\n  "paths": {\n    "/healthz": {\n      "get": {\n        "operationId": "getHealthz",\n        "tags": [\n          "ops"\n        ],\n        "summary": "Liveness probe",\n        "description": "Returns 200 as soon as the process has finished initialising. It checks no\\ndependency (database, cache, queue). Served by every HTTP entry.\\n",\n        "x-auth": "none",\n        "security": [],\n        "responses": {\n          "200": {\n            "description": "The process is initialised.",\n            "headers": {\n              "X-Trace-Id": {\n                "$ref": "#/components/headers/TraceId"\n              }\n            },\n            "content": {\n              "application/json": {\n                "schema": {\n                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HealthzResponse"\n                },\n                "example": {\n                  "code": 0,\n                  "msg": "",\n                  "data": {\n                    "status": "ok",\n                    "entry": "api",\n                    "now": "2026-10-01T04:00:00.000Z"\n                  },\n                  "trace_id": "0199a3b4-5c6d-7e8f-9a0b-1c2d3e4f5a6b"\n                }\n              }\n            }\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    "/v1/devices": {\n      "post": {\n        "operationId": "registerDevice",\n        "tags": [\n          "identity"\n        ],\n        "summary": "Register a device",\n        "description": "Issues `device_id` and `install_secret` after the user has agreed to the privacy policy\\n(BR-ID-09). The client stores install_secret only in Keychain / Keystore / HUKS and signs\\nlater requests with it. Not signed: the device has no secret yet.\\n`device_hash` is lowercase_hex(SHA-256(UTF-8 bytes of the identifier with surrounding\\nwhitespace removed, lower-cased)) and `id_source` names the identifier (BR-ID-09 细则\\n「设备标识的无效值」; MVP Android uses ANDROID_ID only). The client never hashes an invalid\\nidentifier (empty, all zeros, wrong format). A hash of the wrong format, or one on the\\ninvalid-hash list (config device.invalid_hashes), is 20001 with `data.fields=[device_hash]`\\nand no device_id is issued; the client shows nothing and reads the identifier again\\ninstead of retrying the same value. Reaching the per-IP hourly registration limit is 42901\\nwith Retry-After (BR-ID-05 细则「发码与设备注册的风控默认值」).\\n`id_source` is required (04 §6.1, §3.2 devices). Making it required is not a breaking\\nchange: the operation is still planned (no route, no caller), and the oasdiff check leaves\\nplanned operations out of the base contract (tools/ci/oasdiff-base.ts).\\nVersion gate: not applied (session recovery, BR-ID-01 细则 interface table). Session scopes:\\naccepts deletion_only (BR-ID-01 细则「受限会话」).\\n",\n        "x-auth": "none",\n        "x-signed": false,\n        "x-idempotent": false,\n        "x-min-version-gate": false,\n        "x-session-scopes": [\n          "full",\n          "deletion_only"\n        ],\n        "x-error-codes": [\n          20001\n        ],\n        "security": [],\n        "parameters": [\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/AppId"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/Platform"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/AppVersion"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/Build"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/Channel"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/TraceId"\n          }\n        ],\n        "requestBody": {\n          "required": true,\n          "content": {\n            "application/json": {\n              "schema": {\n                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/RegisterDeviceRequest"\n              },\n              "example": {\n                "device_hash": "9f86d081884c7d659a2feaa0c55ad015a3bf4f1b2b0b822cd15d6c15b0f00a08",\n                "id_source": "idfv"\n              }\n            }\n          }\n        },\n        "responses": {\n          "200": {\n            "description": "Device registered.",\n            "headers": {\n              "X-Trace-Id": {\n                "$ref": "#/components/headers/TraceId"\n              }\n            },\n            "content": {\n              "application/json": {\n                "schema": {\n                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/RegisterDeviceResponse"\n                },\n                "example": {\n                  "code": 0,\n                  "msg": "",\n                  "data": {\n                    "device_id": "0199a3b4-5c6d-7e8f-9a0b-1c2d3e4f5a60",\n                    "install_secret": "example-install-secret-value"\n                  },\n                  "trace_id": "0199a3b4-5c6d-7e8f-9a0b-1c2d3e4f5a6b"\n                }\n              }\n            }\n          },\n          "429": {\n            "$ref": "#/components/responses/TooManyRequests"\n          },\n          "4XX": {\n            "$ref": "#/components/responses/ClientError"\n          },\n          "5XX": {\n            "$ref": "#/components/responses/ServerError"\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    "/v1/devices/push-token": {\n      "post": {\n        "operationId": "reportPushToken",\n        "tags": [\n          "identity"\n        ],\n        "summary": "Report the push token of this device",\n        "description": "Writes push_tokens through the notification module. The token value and its binding are\\nwritten only when the calling session is the latest login session of this device;\\notherwise the report is ignored. A token value already registered on another device row\\nis taken over or not according to device registration order and session creation time;\\na holder row that changed hands within the conflict window is frozen and reports during\\nthe freeze are not written (BR-ID-07 细则「推送令牌与会话」). Every case answers success.\\nThe client reports once after each successful login with the new session. provider is a\\nstring until the push provider is chosen (orchestrator decision D-14).\\n",\n        "x-auth": "login",\n        "x-signed": false,\n        "x-idempotent": false,\n        "x-min-version-gate": true,\n        "x-error-codes": [\n          10405\n        ],\n        "security": [\n          {\n            "bearerAuth": []\n          }\n        ],\n        "parameters": [\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/AppId"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/Platform"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/AppVersion"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/Build"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/Channel"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/TraceId"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/DeviceId"\n          }\n        ],\n        "requestBody": {\n          "required": true,\n          "content": {\n            "application/json": {\n              "schema": {\n                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ReportPushTokenRequest"\n              },\n              "example": {\n                "provider": "placeholder-provider",\n                "token": "placeholder-push-token"\n              }\n            }\n          }\n        },\n        "responses": {\n          "200": {\n            "description": "Accepted (also when the report was ignored).",\n            "headers": {\n              "X-Trace-Id": {\n                "$ref": "#/components/headers/TraceId"\n              }\n            },\n            "content": {\n              "application/json": {\n                "schema": {\n                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/EmptyResponse"\n                },\n                "example": {\n                  "code": 0,\n                  "msg": "",\n                  "data": {},\n                  "trace_id": "0199a3b4-5c6d-7e8f-9a0b-1c2d3e4f5a6b"\n                }\n              }\n            }\n          },\n          "429": {\n            "$ref": "#/components/responses/TooManyRequests"\n          },\n          "4XX": {\n            "$ref": "#/components/responses/ClientError"\n          },\n          "5XX": {\n            "$ref": "#/components/responses/ServerError"\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    "/v1/auth/sms-codes": {\n      "post": {\n        "operationId": "sendSmsCode",\n        "tags": [\n          "identity"\n        ],\n        "summary": "Send an SMS verification code",\n        "description": "Order of checks: signature 10401 / 10402 → 30414 (purpose=step_up, action=phone_change, phone\\nchange switch off; no SMS, no limit counted) → 20001 → 44001 → 44003 → 42901 (BR-ID-05). Limits per\\nphone: 1 per 60 s, 5 per natural hour (+08:00), 10 per natural day (+08:00); a code is 6 digits\\nand valid 5 minutes.\\n`phone` is normalised by the server (BR-ID-05 细则「手机号规范化」); when the result is not\\na mainland mobile number the answer is 20001 with `data.fields=[phone]` and\\n`data.reason=phone_invalid`, no SMS is sent and nothing counts towards the limits.\\nVersion gate (conditional, the table of BR-ID-01 细则 rules): not applied when purpose=login,\\nor purpose=step_up with action=account_deletion; applied otherwise (purpose=bind, or step_up\\nwithout action or with another action). Session scopes: a deletion_only session is accepted\\nonly for purpose=login and for purpose=step_up with action=account_deletion. Both conditions\\nfollow BR-ID-01 细则, which wins on any difference.\\n",\n        "x-auth": "none",\n        "x-signed": true,\n        "x-idempotent": false,\n        "x-min-version-gate": "conditional",\n        "x-session-scopes": [\n          "full",\n          "deletion_only"\n        ],\n        "x-error-codes": [\n          20001,\n          44001,\n          44003,\n          42901,\n          10405,\n          30414\n        ],\n        "security": [],\n        "parameters": [\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/AppId"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/Platform"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/AppVersion"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/Build"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/Channel"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/TraceId"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/DeviceId"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/Timestamp"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/Nonce"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/Sign"\n          }\n        ],\n        "requestBody": {\n          "required": true,\n          "content": {\n            "application/json": {\n              "schema": {\n                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/SendSmsCodeRequest"\n              },\n              "example": {\n                "phone": "13800138000",\n                "purpose": "login"\n              }\n            }\n          }\n        },\n        "responses": {\n          "200": {\n            "description": "The provider accepted the SMS, or its outcome is unknown (counted as sent).",\n            "headers": {\n              "X-Trace-Id": {\n                "$ref": "#/components/headers/TraceId"\n              }\n            },\n            "content": {\n              "application/json": {\n                "schema": {\n                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/SendSmsCodeResponse"\n                },\n                "example": {\n                  "code": 0,\n                  "msg": "",\n                  "data": {\n                    "resend_after_sec": 60,\n                    "expires_in_sec": 300\n                  },\n                  "trace_id": "0199a3b4-5c6d-7e8f-9a0b-1c2d3e4f5a6b"\n                }\n              }\n            }\n          },\n          "429": {\n            "$ref": "#/components/responses/TooManyRequests"\n          },\n          "4XX": {\n            "$ref": "#/components/responses/ClientError"\n          },\n          "5XX": {\n            "$ref": "#/components/responses/ServerError"\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    "/v1/auth/login/sms": {\n      "post": {\n        "operationId": "loginBySms",\n        "tags": [\n          "identity"\n        ],\n        "summary": "Log in (or register) with an SMS code",\n        "description": "Creates the account on first login. The request carries the legal versions the user\\nagreed to and the time of agreement (BR-ID-04). An `invite_code` is ignored for an\\nexisting account; `invite_bind` is present only when a non-empty invite_code was sent\\n(BR-INV-06). Errors: 20002 wrong code, 20003 expired code (BR-ID-05). `phone` is\\nnormalised by the server; a number that does not normalise to a mainland mobile number is\\n20001 with `data.fields=[phone]`, `data.reason=phone_invalid` (BR-ID-05 细则「手机号规范化」).\\nCreating the account checks the same-device registration limit (44001, BR-ID-05).\\nVersion gate: not applied (session recovery). A client below the minimum version gets a\\nrestricted login (BR-ID-01 细则「受限会话」): only an existing account is logged in, invite_code is\\nignored (BR-INV-06 handling for an existing account), nothing is created or bound, and no\\nexisting account → 10405 with data.reason=no_account; the response carries\\nsession_scope=deletion_only. Session scopes: accepts deletion_only.\\n",\n        "x-auth": "none",\n        "x-signed": true,\n        "x-idempotent": false,\n        "x-min-version-gate": false,\n        "x-session-scopes": [\n          "full",\n          "deletion_only"\n        ],\n        "x-error-codes": [\n          20001,\n          20002,\n          20003,\n          44001,\n          10405,\n          10007\n        ],\n        "security": [],\n        "parameters": [\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/AppId"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/Platform"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/AppVersion"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/Build"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/Channel"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/TraceId"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/DeviceId"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/Timestamp"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/Nonce"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/Sign"\n          }\n        ],\n        "requestBody": {\n          "required": true,\n          "content": {\n            "application/json": {\n              "schema": {\n                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/LoginBySmsRequest"\n              },\n              "example": {\n                "phone": "13800138000",\n                "code": "123456",\n                "legal_versions": {\n                  "privacy": 3,\n                  "agreement": 2\n                },\n                "consent_at": "2026-10-02T09:30:00+08:00",\n                "invite_code": "K7Q2MZ"\n              }\n            }\n          }\n        },\n        "responses": {\n          "200": {\n            "description": "Logged in.",\n            "headers": {\n              "X-Trace-Id": {\n                "$ref": "#/components/headers/TraceId"\n              }\n            },\n            "content": {\n              "application/json": {\n                "schema": {\n                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/LoginResponse"\n                },\n                "example": {\n                  "code": 0,\n                  "msg": "",\n                  "data": {\n                    "user_id": "0199a3b4-5c6d-7e8f-9a0b-1c2d3e4f5a61",\n                    "is_new_user": true,\n                    "tokens": {\n                      "access_token": "example-access-token-one",\n                      "access_expires_at": "2026-10-02T11:30:00+08:00",\n                      "refresh_token": "example-refresh-token-one",\n                      "refresh_expires_at": "2026-11-01T09:30:00+08:00",\n                      "session_scope": "full"\n                    },\n                    "invite_bind": {\n                      "result": "bound",\n                      "code": null\n                    }\n                  },\n                  "trace_id": "0199a3b4-5c6d-7e8f-9a0b-1c2d3e4f5a6b"\n                }\n              }\n            }\n          },\n          "429": {\n            "$ref": "#/components/responses/TooManyRequests"\n          },\n          "4XX": {\n            "$ref": "#/components/responses/ClientError"\n          },\n          "5XX": {\n            "$ref": "#/components/responses/ServerError"\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    "/v1/auth/oauth-attempts": {\n      "post": {\n        "operationId": "createOauthAttempt",\n        "tags": [\n          "identity"\n        ],\n        "summary": "Get a one-time third-party authorization attempt",\n        "description": "Called before every WeChat, Apple or Huawei authorization (BR-ID-04 细则「第三方身份只信\\n服务端换取或验签的结果」). The attempt is bound to the provider, the purpose and this\\ndevice_id (purpose=step_up also to the user and `action`); it is valid once and for the\\nconfigured lifetime (auth.oauth_attempt_ttl_sec). A submission checks it first and\\nconsumes it only after every check passed. The client passes `nonce` to the provider SDK.\\npurpose=step_up requires a logged-in user (otherwise 10001) and `action`; it is issued only\\nto an account without a bound phone (a bound phone → 20001 with `data.fields=[provider]`,\\nBR-ID-08). purpose=step_up with action=account_deletion is inside the 10006 whitelist\\n(BR-ID-31). purpose=payout_bind (WeChat only, no `action`) is the payout authorization of\\nBR-ID-04 细则「收款授权」 and BR-WDR-33 ②: it requires a logged-in user (otherwise 10001)\\nand is bound to the user, this device_id and this app\'s WeChat AppID; the openid it yields\\nis only stored on the payout account — it creates no account, writes no third-party login\\nbinding and issues or refreshes no token. It is consumed by the payout account save, not by\\na login or step-up submission. purpose=reverify (no `action`) is the re-verification of a\\nrecycled phone (旧号加验, BR-WDR-01 细则): it requires a logged-in user (otherwise 10001), is\\nbound to the user, this device_id and the provider, is consumed only by\\n`POST /v1/me/reverify/oauth`, is available to an account with a bound phone too, and issues\\nno token; a provider that is not among the account\'s trusted identities → 20001 with\\n`data.fields=[provider]`. A deletion_only session is not accepted for it (10405).\\nStorage unavailable → 50001.\\nVersion gate (conditional): not applied when purpose=login, or purpose=step_up with\\naction=account_deletion; applied otherwise. Session scopes: a deletion_only session is\\naccepted only for purpose=login and for purpose=step_up with action=account_deletion. Both\\nper BR-ID-01 细则, which wins on any difference.\\n",\n        "x-auth": "optional",\n        "x-signed": true,\n        "x-idempotent": false,\n        "x-min-version-gate": "conditional",\n        "x-session-scopes": [\n          "full",\n          "deletion_only"\n        ],\n        "x-error-codes": [\n          10001,\n          20001,\n          50001,\n          10405\n        ],\n        "security": [\n          {},\n          {\n            "bearerAuth": []\n          }\n        ],\n        "parameters": [\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/AppId"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/Platform"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/AppVersion"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/Build"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/Channel"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/TraceId"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/DeviceId"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/Timestamp"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/Nonce"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/Sign"\n          }\n        ],\n        "requestBody": {\n          "required": true,\n          "content": {\n            "application/json": {\n              "schema": {\n                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/CreateOauthAttemptRequest"\n              },\n              "example": {\n                "provider": "wechat",\n                "purpose": "login"\n              }\n            }\n          }\n        },\n        "responses": {\n          "200": {\n            "description": "A new attempt.",\n            "headers": {\n              "X-Trace-Id": {\n                "$ref": "#/components/headers/TraceId"\n              }\n       