annel); it carries no\\namount or title: the server prices the order from the business type (BR-PAY-01 ①), and\\nany other field (amount, amount_fen, …) → 20001. The order belongs to the caller: biz_ref\\nmust be the caller\'s own business object.\\n\\nChecks (BR-PAY-01 ④): pay.enabled off → 30901 reason=pay_disabled;\\npay.channel_enabled.<pay_channel> off → 30901 reason=channel_disabled; the client platform\\n(X-Platform) not in pay.biz.<biz_type>.platforms → 30901 reason=platform_not_allowed; the\\nbusiness type or object cannot be sold → 30901 reason=biz_not_sellable. The business\\nobject already has a PAID order → 30902 with data.pay_order_id (BR-PAY-02). It already\\nhas a PENDING order on the same channel: if that order is not in the closing flow\\n(closing=false), the existing (original) order is returned with freshly issued launch\\nparameters instead of a new one; if it is in the closing flow (closing=true: the user\\ncancelled it, or it passed expire_at), no launch parameters are returned any more\\n(BR-PAY-03: once closing, launch parameters are never issued again) and the request gets\\n20902 with data.resource=pay_order; the client waits for the close to finish and then\\norders again. Switching to another channel: the original PENDING order must first be\\ncancelled and closed (BR-PAY-02, BR-PAY-05); a new order is created only after the\\noriginal one is CLOSED. While the original order\'s close has not finished, or the\\nchannel\'s result is unknown, the request gets 20902 with data.resource=pay_order\\n(orchestrator ruling D10-236 ④); if the close finds the original order already paid, it\\ngoes PO2 and the request gets 30902 with data.pay_order_id = the original order. A state\\nCAS that affects no row → 20902 with data.resource=pay_order. Placing the order with the\\nchannel fails or times out → 50306 with data.pay_channel; the order stays PENDING and a\\nretry with the same business object gets launch parameters for it (BR-PAY-03).\\n\\nThe res