ond; the boundary instant itself is\\nrejected) → 30409 (has an order, a claim or a direct invitee, any status) → 30401\\n(normalised code empty, length ≠ 6 or outside the character set; no lookup) → 30401\\n(inviter missing or unavailable) → 30403 (self, own invitee or same device, BR-INV-08).\\n30401 never tells the reason. Every 30401 counts per phone_hmac per natural day\\n(+08:00); once the count reaches invite.fail_limit_per_day (5) the following requests that\\nday stop at the rate-limit step with 42901 and Retry-After up to the next 00:00 +08:00.\\nSucceeds at most once per account: the write is conditional (no inviter and the\\nself-binding chance unused), so of two concurrent requests with different keys exactly one\\nbinds and the other gets 30402. The client fetches GET /v1/me again after success.\\nVersion gate: applied.\\n",\n        "x-auth": "phone",\n        "x-signed": true,\n        "x-idempotent": true,\n        "x-min-version-gate": true,\n        "x-error-codes": [\n          10005,\n          30408,\n          42901,\n          30402,\n          30404,\n          30409,\n          30401,\n          30403,\n          10405\n        ],\n        "security": [\n          {\n            "bearerAuth": []\n          }\n        ],\n        "parameters": [\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/AppId"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/Platform"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/AppVersion"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/Build"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/Channel"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/TraceId"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/DeviceId"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/Timestamp"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/pa