h",\n        "tags": [\n          "admin-search"\n        ],\n        "summary": "Top-bar search by a full order number, withdrawal number, phone number or UID",\n        "description": "The console\'s top-bar search (01 F-ADM-04; 04 §6.6 search; BR-ID-34 细则「一框搜」). Any\\nsigned-in admin may call it (read only, no step-up); what comes back is trimmed by the\\nserver to three permission points, one per hit type (enum admin_search_hit_type): order\\n`order.view`, user `user.lookup`, withdrawal `fund.view`. A super admin holds every point.\\n\\n`q` is trimmed of surrounding whitespace and must then be 1–64 characters, else 20001 with\\n`data.fields=[q]`. The server tells from its shape what `q` is and matches the full value\\nonly (no prefix or partial match): an order number (the order\'s full number), a withdrawal\\nnumber (its full number; no hit until the withdrawal module ships), a full phone number\\n(normalised as in BR-ID-05 细则「手机号规范化」) or a UID (the user_id, a UUID). Only\\nobjects of the console\'s app are found. Input of no recognised shape is not an error: 200\\nwith an empty list.\\n\\nAnti-probing (BR-ID-34 细则「一框搜」): no hit and no permission look the same. A hit of a\\ntype the account has no point for is dropped silently; when nothing is left the response is\\n200 with `items=[]` and `truncated=false`. The operation never answers 10403\\n`admin_permission_denied` (10403 only for `admin_ip_not_allowed`, common to every admin\\noperation) and never 20001 for an unknown number, unlike GET /admin/v1/users/lookup.\\n\\n`items[]` lists the hits (`type`, `id` for the detail route, `summary` a masked one-line\\nsummary: phone numbers masked 3 + 4 as BR-ID-33, no full phone, identity or payout account\\nnumber). An order or withdrawal hit is followed by its owner as a `user` item, trimmed by\\n`user.lookup` like any user hit. At most 10 items; when there are more, the first 10 come\\nback with `truncated=true` (the console asks for a more complete number). The console\\nopens the detail page directly when exactly one item comes back and lists candidates\\notherwise.\\n\\nAudit: a search by full phone number that returns a user writes an audit entry, as a\\nlookup by phone through `user.lookup` does (04 §6.6 search). Other searches are not\\naudited.\\n",\n        "x-auth": "admin",\n        "x-implementation": "planned",\n        "x-error-codes": [\n          10001,\n          20001\n        ],\n        "security": [\n          {\n            "adminBearerAuth": []\n          }\n        ],\n        "parameters": [\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/TraceId"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/AdminSearchQuery"\n          }\n        ],\n        "responses": {\n          "200": {\n            "description": "The hits the account may see; empty for no hit and for no permission alike.",\n            "headers": {\n              "X-Trace-Id": {\n                "$ref": "#/components/headers/TraceId"\n              }\n            },\n            "content": {\n              "application/json": {\n                "schema": {\n                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/AdminSearchResponse"\n                },\n                "examples": {\n                  "orderWithOwner": {\n                    "summary": "An order number hit, followed by its owner (order.view and user.lookup)",\n                    "value": {\n                      "code": 0,\n                      "msg": "",\n                      "data": {\n                        "items": [\n                          {\n                            "type": "order",\n                            "id": "0199a3b4-5c6d-7e8f-9a0b-1c2d3e4f6a01",\n                            "summary": "淘宝 订单 3876512094471023 · 已付款"\n                          },\n                          {\n                            "type": "user",\n                            "id": "0199a3b4-5c6d-7e8f-9a0b-1c2d3e4f5c01",\n                            "