he number of one of the claim\'s child\\norders. A `user_id` that names no user of the app, or a filter set nothing matches, is an\\nempty page (`items=[]`, `total=0`), not an error; `counts` still follows its own rule\\nbelow (every filter except `status`), so a `status` nothing matches leaves the other\\ncounts as they are (a user with 3 approved claims and none rejected, read with\\n`status=rejected`: `items=[]`, `total=0`, `counts.approved=3`), and every count is 0 only\\nwhen the filters other than `status` match nothing. A value outside an enum is 20001 with\\n`data.fields` naming the parameter.\\n\\nOrder: claims with status `auto_matched` first (BR-ATTR-18: kept at the top for the\\nreviewer), then every other claim; within each group `submitted_at` descending, then the\\nserver\'s internal order for the same time. Pages with `page` (any positive integer, as\\nAdminPage; a page past the last one is `items=[]`) and `page_size` ≤ 200 (a `page_size`\\nabove 200 is 20001, as AdminPageSize). `counts` has one entry per claim_status value (0 included), counted with\\nevery filter of the request except `status`, so the console\'s status tabs show what each\\ntab would hold; `total` is the count of the page\'s own filter set. The applicant is shown\\nas user_id and phone number masked 3 + 4 (BR-ID-33), never the full number. Reading does\\nnot write an audit record.\\n",\n        "x-auth": "admin",\n        "x-error-codes": [\n          10001,\n          10403,\n          20001\n        ],\n        "security": [\n          {\n            "adminBearerAuth": []\n          }\n        ],\n        "parameters": [\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/TraceId"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/AdminPage"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/AdminPageSize"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/AdminClaimPlatformFilter"\n          },\n          {