         "schema": {\n                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ErrorEnvelope"\n                },\n                "examples": {\n                  "unknownClaim": {\n                    "$ref": "#/components/examples/AdminUnknownClaim"\n                  },\n                  "noPermission": {\n                    "$ref": "#/components/examples/AdminPermissionDenied"\n                  },\n                  "tokenExpired": {\n                    "$ref": "#/components/examples/AdminTokenExpired"\n                  }\n                }\n              }\n            }\n          },\n          "5XX": {\n            "$ref": "#/components/responses/ServerError"\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    "/admin/v1/claims/{claim_id}/items/{item_id}/approve": {\n      "post": {\n        "operationId": "adminApproveClaimItem",\n        "tags": [\n          "admin-claims"\n        ],\n        "summary": "Approve one child order of a claim (returns the whole claim after the review)",\n        "description": "Approves one child order (claim_items) of a claim (01 F-ADM-06; 04 §6.6 claims; BR-ATTR-18,\\nBR-ATTR-20). Permission point `order.claim` (04 §11.2) only: an account holding only\\n`user.lookup`, or neither, gets 10403 with `data.reason=admin_permission_denied` (a super\\nadmin holds every point). No step-up. No Idempotency-Key: the console\'s writes rely on the\\nCAS below (04 §6.6). One child order per call; there is no batch approval.\\n\\nRequest: `expected_row_version` is the child order\'s `row_version` from\\nGET /admin/v1/claims/{claim_id}. `reason` is required for approval and rejection alike,\\n5–200 characters (the console may prefill 「证据核实一致」); after trimming surrounding\\nwhitespace it must still have at least 5 characters, else 20001 with\\n`data.fields=[reason]`; it is stored trimmed. An unknown claim_id or a claim of another\\napp → 20001 with `data.fields=[claim_id]`; an unknown item_id, or one that belongs to\\nanother claim → 20001 with `data.fields=[item_id]`. A child order that is already decided\\n(approved, rejected or cancelled, by a reviewer or by the system, such as sync\\nattribution closing it under BR-ATTR-16), or whose `row_version` is no longer\\n`expected_row_version` → 20902 with `data.resource=claim_item`, nothing changed; the\\nconsole refreshes and shows the result.\\n\\nApproval runs in one transaction under BR-ATTR-20: it takes\\npg_advisory_xact_lock(hash(platform, sub_order_id)), the same lock as sync and admin\\nassignment (BR-ATTR-01), re-reads the order with SELECT … FOR UPDATE, and then checks in\\nthis order (BR-ATTR-20 ② before ③):\\n- The order\'s user_id is no longer empty (attributed by sync, by another claim or by an\\n  admin assignment): the order is not written and no commission snapshot is made; the\\n  child order is closed as BR-ATTR-16 says, `cancelled` when that user_id is the\\n  applicant, else `rejected` with `reject_reason=NOT_IN_POOL`. This is not an error: the\\n  answer is 200 with the claim as it is after closing. Signal (no extra field): the\\n  reviewed child order\'s `decision` in the response. A request to approve whose child\\n  order comes back `cancelled`, or `rejected` with NOT_IN_POOL, was closed this way, and\\n  the console tells the reviewer 「订单已被自动归属」.\\n- Else the order\'s rebate_status is VOID: the system rejects the child order with\\n  `reject_reason=ORDER_INVALID` (BR-ATTR-18; a claim never takes a VOID order,\\n  BR-ATTR-17 ④c, BR-ATTR-20 ③), again 200 with the claim; the order is not written.\\n- Else the child order becomes `approved` and the order is attributed to the applicant\\n  as BR-ATTR-20 ③ says: user_id, user_basis=claim, locked=true, platform_status\\n  unchanged, rebate_status out of UNATTRIBUTED by BR-FUND-01 R3, the commission snapshot\\n  under the conditions of BR-ATTR-01 ⑥, order_status_history with source=claim, the\\n  domain event claim.resolved queued in the same transaction, and source backfill\\n  (BR-ATTR-15). Every other pending child order of the same sub order (in claims of other\\n  applicants) is rejected with NOT_IN_POOL in the same transaction (BR-ATTR-18: the first\\n  approval wins).\\nA child order closed by the system (`cancelled`, NOT_IN_POOL, ORDER_INVALID) has\\n`decided_by` null, as GET /admin/v1/claims/{claim_id} describes; an approval has the\\nreviewer.\\n\\nIn every outcome the child order\'s `row_version` goes up by 1 and `decided_at` is set,\\n`reason` is written to claims.reason (the latest note, shown as the claim\'s `reason`) and\\nto the audit log together with the operator and the outcome; child orders have no note\\nof their own. When every child order of the claim is decided, the claim\'s `status` is\\nsummarized (BR-ATTR-18: any approved → approved; else any rejected → rejected; else\\ncancelled); while one is pending it stays as it is. The applicant is told the result by\\nin-app message and push (BR-ATTR-18). The response is the whole claim after the review,\\nthe same shape as GET /admin/v1/claims/{claim_id}.\\n",\n        "x-auth": "admin",\n        "x-error-codes": [\n          10001,\n          10403,\n          20001,\n          20902\n        ],\n        "security": [\n          {\n            "adminBearerAuth": []\n          }\n        ],\n        "parameters": [\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/TraceId"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/AdminClaimIdPath"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/AdminClaimItemIdPath"\n          }\n        ],\n        "requestBody": {\n          "required": true,\n          "content": {\n            "application/json": {\n              "schema": {\n                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/AdminApproveClaimItemRequest"\n              },\n              "example": {\n                "expected_row_version": 0,\n                "reason": "证据核实一致"\n              }\n            }\n          }\n        },\n       