ason names (admin_dict)",\n        "description": "Permission: any permission point (04 §6.6 `dict`; any signed-in console account holding at\\nleast one permission point; read only, no step-up; no new permission point). The console\\ndictionary of BR-TEXT-25: the Chinese names the console shows for statuses and reasons,\\nevery `admin_dict.*` key, whose bundled defaults are contracts/texts.admin.default.json\\n(console only, not bundled in the App or H5). Unlike GET /v1/dict, every key is returned:\\nits current override, or its bundled default when not overridden. A key\\n`admin_dict.<enum>.<code>` is items[enum][code]: the `admin_dict.` prefix is dropped and\\nthe rest split at its last dot (`enum` is the 04 enum name or `table.column` and may hold\\ndots, e.g. `admin_adjustments.status`; `code` is the 04 value with its case). The console\\nshows the code itself when a key is missing (BR-TEXT-25). `version` is the dictionary\'s\\ncurrent version, as GET /v1/dict (\\"0\\" before the first publish). Not paged. Read only;\\ntexts are changed on the dictionary page through PUT /admin/v1/dict-items, by key class\\n(fund term keys → `content.fund_terms`, other keys → `config.general`, as classified in\\nspecs/fund-term-keys.yaml).\\n",\n        "x-auth": "admin",\n        "x-error-codes": [\n          10001,\n          10403\n        ],\n        "security": [\n          {\n            "adminBearerAuth": []\n          }\n        ],\n        "parameters": [\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/TraceId"\n          }\n        ],\n        "responses": {\n          "200": {\n            "description": "Every console dictionary key, by enum and code.",\n            "headers": {\n              "X-Trace-Id": {\n                "$ref": "#/components/headers/TraceId"\n              }\n            },\n            "content": {\n              "application/json": {\n                "schema": {\n                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/AdminDictResponse"\n