en` is not looked at.\\n\\nEffects, in one transaction under the member\'s balance lock. `available` below 0: the\\nvoucher BAD_DEBT_WRITEOFF with uniq_key `BADDEBT:{account_id}:{id}` debits BAD_DEBT and\\ncredits USER_BALANCE.available by −`available` (the current amount), which brings\\n`available` to 0; the candidate becomes APPROVED with `approver_id` the caller,\\n`approved_at` and `voucher_id` set; the linked accounts (same real name, device or payee\\naccount) get their risk mark. `available` at 0 or above: the candidate becomes CANCELLED,\\nwith no voucher, no risk mark, `approver_id` and `approved_at` staying null, and the\\nanswer is still 200 with `written_off_fen=0`. Writes an audit record (action\\nbad_debt_writeoff_approve, with the `id`, the `account_id`, the resulting status,\\n`written_off_fen` and `available` before and after; no personal data). Later credits\\ncount towards the balance as usual; nothing is pursued afterwards.\\n\\n`Idempotency-Key` is required: same key and body → the first result; same key with\\nanother body → 20901; same key while still running → 40901. The step-up token is a header\\nand not part of the body hash, so a replay after a 10003 keeps its key.\\n",\n        "x-auth": "admin",\n        "x-idempotent": true,\n        "x-implementation": "planned",\n        "x-error-codes": [\n          10001,\n          10003,\n          10403,\n          20001,\n          20901,\n          20902,\n          40901\n        ],\n        "security": [\n          {\n            "adminBearerAuth": []\n          }\n        ],\n        "parameters": [\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/TraceId"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/AdminBadDebtWriteoffIdPath"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/AdminStepUpToken"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/IdempotencyKey"\n          }\n        ],\n        "requestBody":