out one → 10003 with `data.tier=totp`. Entering and confirming are one\\nsubmission and one person may do both, also the reviewer (BR-WDR-16, ADD-05);\\n`manual_entry_by` and `manual_confirm_by` are both the caller. A separate confirmation step\\nis not offered.\\n\\nRequest (AdminWithdrawalBatchManualPaidRequest): `items`, 1 to 200 (200 is 代理补全的默认,\\nD10-595), each with `withdrawal_id`, `channel_order_id` (the Alipay or bank transfer serial\\nnumber, by the withdrawal\'s snapshot channel; 1 to 64 characters with no whitespace, so that\\na stray space cannot make the same number look new, and no NUL, which the database cannot\\nstore; compared exactly, case included),\\n`paid_at` (when the money was really paid) and `paid_fen` (integer fen, the amount really\\npaid; any integer reaches the item\'s own check). A withdrawal may appear only once: a duplicate `withdrawal_id` is 20001 with\\n`data.fields=[items]`.\\n\\nOrder of checks: the route schema comes first, before the permission and step-up checks, as\\non every admin route (D10-591): a body that fails it is 20001 with `data.fields` naming the\\nfield, also for a caller without the permission point or a token, and nothing is written.\\nThen `payout.manual_entry` (10403 with `data.reason=admin_permission_denied`) → step-up\\n(10003) → the duplicate check. After that the answer is 200 and each item has its own\\nresult: an item that cannot be recorded never fails the others.\\n\\nEach item runs in its own transaction, in the order given, under the member\'s locks and the\\nwithdrawal\'s row lock, and the first check that fails is its result, in `items`, one per\\nrequest item in request order: `paid`, or `skipped` with `reason`:\\n\\n- `not_found`: an unknown id, one of another app, or one that is not a UUID (which never\\n  reaches the database).\\n- `not_approved`: not APPROVED. W8 starts only there (BR-WDR-16). EXECUTE and W8 both\\n  require APPROVED under a CAS, and the first to commit wins, so the loser gets this and\\n  no money moves twice.\\n- `channel_not_allowed`: a wechat withdrawal; W8 is not open to it (BR-WDR-33 ⑧).\\n- `amount_mismatch`: `paid_fen` is not exactly the withdrawal\'s `net_fen` (BR-WDR-16).\\n- `paid_at_invalid`: `paid_at` is more than 5 minutes after the injected Clock, or before\\n  the withdrawal\'s `created_at` (代理补全的默认: no one can pay in the future or before the\\n  member asked, and the tax export and the watermark read this time).\\n- `has_transfer_attempt`: a kind=transfer attempt with result pending, success or unknown.\\n  That money may be out, so such a withdrawal ends through BR-WDR-15. An attempt that\\n  definitely failed does not stop W8.\\n- `query_required` or `query_success`: while the switch\\n  `payout.proven_success_writeoff.enabled` is on (default on), a withdrawal with\\n  `hold_reason=payer_side_after_transfer` is checked against its latest query, because a\\n  transfer the channel reported as failed may still have been paid (BR-WDR-08 W8,\\n  BR-WDR-17, 决-08 A). No query yet, or a latest query with an unknown result, is\\n  `query_required`. A latest query that succeeded is `query_success`: the channel paid, so\\n  this withdrawal ends through W11, and recording an offline payment too would pay twice. A\\n  latest query with result fail lets it through. BR-WDR-17 also allows 「订单不存在」, but that\\n  answer is recorded with result unknown and has no verified channel code yet (BR-WDR-22,\\n  BR-WDR-28), so until one is registered it is `query_required`: the safe direction. With\\n  the switch off this check does not run.\\n- `member_blocked`: a withdrawal block of the member (BR-WDR-05): risk state frozen, banned\\n  or appealing over either, an effective withdraw hold, available below 0, or\\n  `blocked_reason` set.\\n- `channel_order_id_taken`: `(app_id, channel_order_id)` is already on a withdrawal,\\n  whichever way it was paid, and also an earlier item of this request; two requests racing\\n  for one number are settled by