e of another app is 20001 with `data.fields=[withdrawal_id]`\\n(no 404) → a withdrawal that is neither of the two below is 20902 with\\n`data.resource=withdrawal`.\\n\\nTwo kinds of withdrawal can be queried: PAYING with `needs_manual=true` (automatic queries\\nhave stopped, BR-WDR-14), and APPROVED with `hold_reason=payer_side_after_transfer`, which\\nhas no other way to get a query recorded and needs one before W3 or W8 (BR-WDR-17, D10-596 ①).\\n\\nThe job asks the channel once, on the withdrawal\'s own out_biz_no, and only appends one\\nkind=query attempt. **It moves nothing:** no status change even on a success or a definite\\nfailure, no voucher, no next query point, no second transfer (BR-WDR-14). A person ends the\\nwithdrawal through adminResolveUnknownPayout, W3, W8 or W11. 「订单不存在」 is recorded as result\\nunknown until its channel code is verified (BR-WDR-22, BR-WDR-28).\\n\\nWrites an audit record (action payout_query_request, with the `withdrawal_id`, the status and\\nno personal data) on the transaction that queues the job. `Idempotency-Key` is required:\\nsame key and body → the first answer and no second job; same key with another body → 20901;\\nsame key while still running → 40901. A new key queries again. The step-up token is a header\\nand not part of the body hash, so a replay after a 10003 keeps its key.\\n",\n        "x-auth": "admin",\n        "x-idempotent": true,\n        "x-error-codes": [\n          10001,\n          10003,\n          10403,\n          20001,\n          20901,\n          20902,\n          40901\n        ],\n        "security": [\n          {\n            "adminBearerAuth": []\n          }\n        ],\n        "parameters": [\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/TraceId"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/AdminStepUpToken"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/IdempotencyKey"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/AdminWithdrawalIdPath"\n          }\n        ],\n        "requestBody": {\n          "required": true,\n          "content": {\n            "application/json": {\n              "schema": {\n                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/AdminPayoutQueryRequest"\n              },\n              "example": {}\n            }\n          }\n        },\n        "responses": {\n          "200": {\n            "description": "The query is queued, or the first answer of the same key.",\n            "headers": {\n              "X-Trace-Id": {\n                "$ref": "#/components/headers/TraceId"\n              }\n            },\n            "content": {\n              "application/json": {\n                "schema": {\n                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/AdminPayoutQueryResponse"\n                },\n                "example": {\n                  "code": 0,\n                  "msg": "",\n                  "data": {\n                    "withdrawal_id": "0199a3b4-5c6d-7e8f-9a0b-1c2d3e4fc001",\n                    "result": "submitted"\n                  },\n                  "trace_id": "0199a3b4-5c6d-7e8f-9a0b-1c2d3e4f5a6b"\n                }\n              }\n            }\n          },\n          "429": {\n            "$ref": "#/components/responses/TooManyRequests"\n          },\n          "4XX": {\n            "description": "Not processed (codes in contracts/error-codes.yaml).",\n            "headers": {\n              "X-Trace-Id": {\n                "$ref": "#/components/headers/TraceId"\n              }\n            },\n            "content": {\n              "application/json": {\n                "schema": {\n                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ErrorEnvelope"\n                },\n                "examples": {\n                  "stepUpRequired": {\n                    "$ref": "#/components/examples/AdminStepUpRequiredTotp"\n                  },\n                  "noPermission": {\n                    "$ref": "#/components/examples/AdminPermissionDenied"\n                  },\n                  "tokenExpired": {\n                    "$ref": "#/components/examples/AdminTokenExpired"\n                  }\n                }\n              }\n            }\n          },\n          "5XX": {\n            "$ref": "#/components/responses/ServerError"\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    "/admin/v1/withdrawals/{withdrawal_id}/resolve": {\n      "post": {\n        "operationId": "adminResolveUnknownPayout",\n        "tags": [\n          "admin-withdrawals"\n        ],\n        "summary": "End a withdrawal whose result stayed unknown (W10, 未知结果处置)",\n        "description": "The 【确认处置】 of the disposal page (BR-WDR-15, BR-WDR-08 W10, BR-WDR-09, BR-WDR-14; rulings\\nD10-595, D10-625, D10-626). Permission point `payout.execute`; a super admin holds every point;\\none person may do it (ADD-05). Step-up: totp tier (BR-ID-34): without a valid totp-tier\\n`X-Step-Up-Token` → 10003 with `data.tier=totp`.\\n\\nRequest (AdminUnknownPayoutResolveRequest): `resolution`, `paid` or `failed`; `proof_text`,\\nthe pasted proof, the query answer or the bill line naming this out_biz_no, 1 to 4000\\ncharacters and not blank after trimming (text only, no file upload, D10-595 ②; stored in\\n`proof_file` and not shown to the member). With `paid`, also `channel_order_id` (1 to 64\\ncharacters, no whitespace or NUL, compared exactly) and `paid_at` (when the channel paid).\\n\\nOrder of checks: the route schema first, as on every admin route (D10-591). Then\\n`payout.execute` (10403 with `data.reason=admin_permission_denied`) → step-up (10003) →\\na blank `proof_text`, or `paid` without `channel_order_id` or `paid_at`, is 20001 with\\n`data.fields` naming them → an unknown `withdrawal_id` or one of another app is 20001 with\\n`data.fields=[withdrawal_id]` (no 404) → a withdrawal not PAYING with `needs_manual=true`, or\\nchanged by another request, is 20902 with `data.resource=withdrawal`. A `needs_manual`\\nwithdrawal never becomes PAID_MANUAL and is never transferred again (BR-WDR-15).\\n\\n**`paid`** (the proof shows the channel succeeded): while the latest kind=query attempt has\\nresult fail and `recon_channel` has no success line for this out_biz_no, 20001 with\\n`data.fields=[resolution]` and `data.reason=resolve_query_failed`: the channel said the\\ntransfer failed and nothing contradicts it, so telling the member the money arrived could be\\nfalse, and the bill reconciliation of that day would not catch it afterwards. A later query\\nor a bill line lifts this; the money stays frozen meanwhile. `paid_at` more than 5 minutes\\nafter the injected Clock, or before T, is 20001 with `data.fields=[paid_at]` and\\n`data.reason=resolve_paid_at_invalid`; a `channel_order_id` already on another withdrawal is\\n20001 with `data.fields=[channel_order_id]` and `data.reason=resolve_order_id_taken`, also\\nwhen two requests race and the unique index settles it. Otherwise, on one transaction: W10 to\\nPAID_API with `paid_at`, `channel_order_id`, `manual_resolution=paid`, `resolver_ids` the caller\\nand `proof_file`; the success voucher of W5 (`wd:{withdrawal_id}:PAID`, the snapshot channel\'s\\ncash subject, BR-WDR-09); `tax_ytd` (BR-WDR-20); wallet.withdrawal_changed, which sends the\\nmember the result message; and an audit record (action withdrawal_resolve, with the\\n`withdrawal_id`, the status before and after, `resolution`, `channel_order_id` and `paid_at`; no\\npersonal data and not the proof text). A member without a verified real name fails `tax_ytd`:\\n20001 with `data.fields=[withdrawal_id]` and `data.reason=resolve_identity_missing`, nothing\\nwritten, because the money was paid and this needs a person.\\n\\n**`failed`** (BR-WDR-15): refunding money that actually left is a double payment, so every\\ncondition is checked by the server and nothing in the request can vouch for one. In order,\\nthe first that does not hold is 20001 with `data.fields=[resolution]` and its `data.reason`:\\n\\n- `resolve_too_early`: less than 24 hours since T.\\n- `resolve_bill_unverifiable`: the bills of T\'s day and the next must both be downloaded and\\n  both lack this out_biz_no. There is no read yet that tells a downloaded bill without this\\n  line from a bill not downloaded, and not finding a line is never taken as absent.\\n- `resolve_query_unverifiable`: the latest query must be 「订单不存在」. That answer has no\\n  verified channel code yet and is recorded as unknown (BR-WDR-22, BR-WDR-28).\\n\\n**So today every `failed` is refused, and nothing is written (D10-625, D10-626).** The target,\\nonce the bill read and the code exist, is W10 to FAILED with `WITHDRAW:RETURN` and a\\n`withdraw_holds` row (`manual_failed_watch`, `withdraw.manual_failed_hold_days`, default 7) on\\none transaction; that path comes with its own task and rule tests before the Alipay channel\\nopens. A wechat withdrawal has its own conditions (BR-WDR-33 ⑧) and is refused the same way\\nuntil then.\\n\\n`Idempotency-Key` is required: same key and body → the first result; same key with another\\nbody → 20901; same key while still running → 40901. 2xxxx refusals are not stored, so a fixed\\nrequest can reuse its key. The step-up token is a header and not part of the body hash, so a\\nreplay after a 10003 keeps its key.\\n",\n        "x-auth": "admin",\n        "x-idempotent": true,\n        "x-error-codes": [\n          10001,\n          10003,\n          10403,\n          20001,\n          20901,\n          20902,\n          40901\n        ],\n        "security": [\n          {\n            "adminBearerAuth": []\n          }\n        ],\n        "parameters": [\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/TraceId"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/AdminStepUpToken"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/IdempotencyKey"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/AdminWithdrawalIdPath"\n          }\n        ],\n        "requestBody": {\n          "required": true,\n          "content": {\n            "application/json": {\n              "schema": {\n                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/AdminUnknownPayoutResolveRequest"\n              },\n              "examples": {\n                "paid": {\n                  "summary": "The proof shows the channel paid",\n                  "value": {\n                    "resolution": "paid",\n                    "proof_text": "账单行：out_biz_no=W20261103001，成功，9800 分",\n                    "channel_order_id": "20261103220014001",\n                    "paid_at": "2026-11-03T09:30:00+08:00"\n                  }\n                },\n                "failed": {\n                  "summary": "Refused today; see the description",\n                  "value": {\n                    "resolution": "failed",\n                    "proof_text": "查询返回订单不存在；当日与次日账单都没有"\n                  }\n                }\n              }\n            }\n          }\n        },\n        "responses": {\n          "200": {\n            "description": "The withdrawal ended, or the first result of the same key.",\n            "headers": {\n              "X-Trace-Id": {\n                "$ref": "#/components/headers/TraceId"\n              }\n            },\n            "content": {\n              "application/json": {\n                "schema": {\n                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/AdminUnknownPayoutResolveResponse"\n                },\n                "example": {\n                  "code": 0,\n                  "msg": "",\n                  "data": {\n                    "withdrawal_id": "0199a3b4-5c6d-7e8f-9a0b-1c2d3e4fc001",\n                    "status": "PAID_API",\n                    "manual_resolution": "paid",\n                    "channel_order_id": "20261103220014001",\n                    "paid_at": "2026-11-03T09:30:00+08:00"\n                  },\n                  "trace_id": "0199a3b4-5c6d-7e8f-9a0b-1c2d3e4f5a6b"\n                }\n              }\n            }\n          },\n          "429": {\n            "$ref": "#/components/responses/TooManyRequests"\n          },\n          "4XX": {\n            "description": "Not processed (codes in contracts/error-codes.yaml).",\n            "headers": {\n              "X-Trace-Id": {\n                "$ref": "#/components/headers/TraceId"\n              }\n            },\n            "content": {\n              "application/json": {\n                "schema": {\n                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ErrorEnvelope"\n                },\n                "examples": {\n                  "stepUpRequired": {\n                    "$ref": "#/components/examples/AdminStepUpRequiredTotp"\n                  },\n                  "noPermission": {\n                    "$ref": "#/components/examples/AdminPermissionDenied"\n                  },\n                  "tokenExpired": {\n                    "$ref": "#/components/examples/AdminTokenExpired"\n                  }\n                }\n              }\n            }\n          },\n          "5XX": {\n            "$ref": "#/components/responses/ServerError"\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    "/admin/v1/withdrawals/{withdrawal_id}/reject": {\n      "post": {\n        "operationId": "adminRejectWithdrawal",\n        "tags": [\n          "admin-withdrawals"\n        ],\n        "summary": "Reject one withdrawal and return its money to the balance (驳回)",\n        "description": "The 【驳回】 of the withdrawal review page and detail (01 F-ADM-07; BR-WDR-10, BR-WDR-09;\\ndesign/specs/admin-withdrawals.md; ruling D10-595). Permission point `withdraw.review`; a\\nsuper admin holds every point. Step-up: totp tier (BR-ID-34): without a valid totp-tier\\n`X-Step-Up-Token` → 10003 with `data.tier=totp`.\\n\\nRequest (AdminWithdrawalRejectRequest): `reason_code`, one of the five a person can choose\\n(RISK_SUSPECT, ORDER_ABNORMAL, PAYEE_INFO_INVALID, USER_REQUEST, OTHER); NEGATIVE_BALANCE\\nis written by the system only and fails at the schema. `note`, the internal note, at most\\n500 characters and not blank after trimming, required for USER_REQUEST (BR-WDR-10: a member\\ncancels through customer service, and the reason must be recorded). The member sees the text\\nof the reason code, never the note.\\n\\nOrder of checks: the route schema comes first, before the permission and step-up checks, as\\non every admin route (D10-591): a body that fails it is 20001 with `data.fields` naming the\\nfield, also for a caller without the permission point or a token, and nothing is written.\\nThen `withdraw.review` (10403 with `data.reason=admin_permission_denied`) → step-up (10003) →\\na blank `note`, or none for USER_REQUEST, is 20001 with `data.fields=[note]` → an unknown\\n`withdrawal_id` or one of another app is 20001 with `data.fields=[withdrawal_id]` (no 404) →\\na withdrawal not in PENDING_REVIEW or APPROVED, or changed by another request, is 20902 with\\n`data.resource=withdrawal` (refresh) → a transfer attempt with result pending, success or\\nunknown is 20001 with `data.fields=[withdrawal_id]` and `data.reason=reject_attempt_exists`:\\nsuch a withdrawal ends only through BR-WDR-15 → while the switch\\n`payout.proven_success_writeoff.enabled` is on (default on), a withdrawal with\\n`hold_reason=payer_side_after_transfer` is checked against its latest query, because a\\ntransfer the channel reported as failed may still have been paid (BR-WDR-08 W3, BR-WDR-17,\\n决-08 A): no query yet, or a latest query with an unknown result, is 20001 with\\n`data.fields=[withdrawal_id]` and `data.reason=reject_query_required`; a latest query that\\nsucceeded is 20001 with `data.reason=reject_query_success`: the money went out, so this\\nwithdrawal ends through W11 and rejecting it would pay twice. A latest query with result\\nfail, a status `payout.query_status_map` maps to a definite failure (BR-WDR-28), lets the\\nrejection through. BR-WDR-17 also allows 「订单不存在」, but that answer is recorded with result\\nunknown and has no verified channel code yet (BR-WDR-22, BR-WDR-28), so until one is\\nregistered it is refused as reject_query_required like every other unknown result: the\\nsafe direction. `payout.payer_side_codes` is also empty until verified, so no withdrawal\\nreaches this state before then. With the switch off this check does not run. Apart from\\nthese, a transfer attempt that definitely failed does not stop a rejection.\\n\\nEffects, in one transaction under the member\'s balance lock: W3 with `reject_reason_code`,\\n`reject_note`, `reviewer_id` the caller and `reviewed_at` the injected Clock; the voucher\\nWITHDRAW:RETURN moving the amount from frozen back to available (BR-WDR-09);\\nwallet.withdrawal_changed, from which the member gets the rejection message. Writes an audit\\nrecord (action withdrawal_reject, with the `withdrawal_id`, the status before and after, the\\n`reason_code` and the `note`; no personal data).\\n\\n`Idempotency-Key` is required: same key and body → the first result; same key with\\nanother body → 20901; same key while still running → 40901. A new key for a withdrawal\\nalready rejected is 20902. The step-up token is a header and not part of the body hash, so\\na replay after a 10003 keeps its key.\\n",\n        "x-auth": "admin",\n        "x-idempotent": true,\n        "x-error-codes": [\n          10001,\n          10003,\n          10403,\n          20001,\n          20901,\n          20902,\n          40901\n        ],\n        "security": [\n          {\n            "adminBearerAuth": []\n          }\n        ],\n        "parameters": [\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/TraceId"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/AdminStepUpToken"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/IdempotencyKey"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/AdminWithdrawalIdPath"\n          }\n        ],\n        "requestBody": {\n          "required": true,\n          "content": {\n            "application/json": {\n              "schema": {\n                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/AdminWithdrawalRejectRequest"\n              },\n              "example": {\n                "reason_code": "PAYEE_INFO_INVALID",\n                "note": "收款账号实名与绑定信息不一致"\n              }\n            }\n          }\n        },\n        "responses": {\n          "200": {\n            "description": "The withdrawal rejected, or the first result of the same key.",\n            "headers": {\n              "X-Trace-Id": {\n                "$ref": "#/components/headers/TraceId"\n              }\n            },\n            "content": {\n              "application/json": {\n                "schema": {\n                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/AdminWithdrawalRejectResponse"\n                },\n                "example": {\n                  "code": 0,\n                  "msg": "",\n                  "data": {\n                    "withdrawal_id": "0199a3b4-5c6d-7e8f-9a0b-1c2d3e4fc001",\n                    "status": "REJECTED",\n                    "reject_reason_code": "PAYEE_INFO_INVALID",\n                    "reviewer_id": "0199a3b4-5c6d-7e8f-9a0b-1c2d3e4f5b01",\n                    "reviewed_at": "2026-11-03T10:00:00+08:00"\n                  },\n                  "trace_id": "0199a3b4-5c6d-7e8f-9a0b-1c2d3e4f5a6b"\n                }\n              }\n            }\n          },\n          "429": {\n            "$ref": "#/components/responses/TooManyRequests"\n          },\n          "4XX": {\n            "description": "Not rejected (codes in contracts/error-codes.yaml).",\n            "headers": {\n              "X-Trace-Id": {\n                "$ref": "#/components/headers/TraceId"\n              }\n            },\n            "content": {\n              "application/json": {\n                "schema": {\n                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ErrorEnvelope"\n                },\n                "examples": {\n                  "stepUpRequired": {\n                    "$ref": "#/components/examples/AdminStepUpRequiredTotp"\n                  },\n                  "noPermission": {\n                    "$ref": "#/components/examples/AdminPermissionDenied"\n                  },\n                  "tokenExpired": {\n                    "$ref": "#/components/examples/AdminTokenExpired"\n                  }\n                }\n              }\n            }\n          },\n          "5XX": {\n            "$ref": "#/components/responses/ServerError"\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    "/admin/v1/settle-bills": {\n      "get": {\n        "operationId": "listAdminSettleBills",\n        "tags": [\n          "admin-settle-bills"\n        ],\n        "summary": "Monthly settlement bills of the app, page by page, newest bill month first",\n        "description": "The bill list of the settlement console (01 F-ADM-08 月结; 04 §3.2 settle_bills,\\nsettle_batches; design/specs/admin-settle-bills.md §1, §4). Read only, no step-up.\\nPermission point: any of `settle.bill` or `fund.view` (04 §11.1, §11.2); a super admin\\nholds every point. Each row is one settle_bills row of the console\'s app: `bill_id` (the\\nbill month M, YYYY-MM, BR-FUND-04 ③), the derived `status` (enum\\nadmin_settle_bill_status; see AdminSettleBillStatus for the rule and for how the latest\\nround is read from settle_batches — derived at read time, not stored), `generation_started_at`,\\n`generated_at`, the bill-day totals `platform_order_counts`,\\n`platform_settle_commission_totals`, `beneficiary_total_fen`, `platform_retained_fen`,\\n`error_count` and `held_count`, the batch summary (`batch_count`, `draft_batch_count`)\\nand `created_at`.\\n\\nThe totals and the counts `error_count` / `held_count` of settle_bills reflect the\\nbill-day task only; supplement batches do not write them back (编排裁定 D10-280 ③,\\nBR-FUND-04 细则「补充批次」). They are for display only: every amount judgement and\\nreconciliation goes by the batch items (GET /admin/v1/settle-batches/{batch_id}/items),\\nnever by these totals. The differences found by the consistency check (差错单) are not\\nlisted by this resource; they are read through GET /admin/v1/recon-diffs.\\n\\nFilters combine with AND: `bill_from` and `bill_to` (bill months YYYY-MM, both inclusive)\\nand `status` (the derived status at response time). A value outside the enum or the\\npattern is 20001 with `data.fields` naming the parameter; `bill_from` later than\\n`bill_to` is 20001 with `data.fields=[bill_from, bill_to]`. A filter set nothing matches\\nis an empty page (`items=[]`, `total=0`), not an error.\\n\\nOrder: `bill_id` descending. Pages with `page` (as AdminPage; a page past the last one is\\n`items=[]`) and `page_size` ≤ 200 (above 200 is 20001, as AdminPageSize); `total` is the\\ncount of the filter set. The Chinese names of the statuses come from the console\\ndictionary (BR-TEXT-25 admin_dict), not from this contract. Writes (confirm, schedule,\\ncancel a schedule, reject, continue execution, supplement batches, upload, check and\\nimport of a union settlement statement) and the export are not part of this operation.\\nReading does not write an audit record.\\n",\n        "x-auth": "admin",\n        "x-error-codes": [\n          10001,\n          10403,\n          20001\n        ],\n        "security": [\n          {\n            "adminBearerAuth": []\n          }\n        ],\n        "parameters": [\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/TraceId"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/AdminPage"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/AdminPageSize"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/AdminSettleBillFrom"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/AdminSettleBillTo"\n          },\n          {\n            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/AdminSettleBillStatusFilter"\n          }\n        ],\n        "responses": {\n          "200": {\n            "description": "One page of monthly settlement bills, newest bill month first.",\n            "headers": {\n              "X-Trace-Id": {\n                "$ref": "#/components/headers/TraceId"\n              }\n            },\n            "content": {\n              "application/json": {\n                "schema": {\n                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/AdminSettleBillPageResponse"\n                },\n                "example": {\n                  "code": 0,\n                  "msg": "",\n                  "data": {\n                    "items": [\n                      {\n                        "bill_id": "2026-09",\n                        "status": "issued",\n                        "generation_started_at": "2026-10-24T02:00:00+08:00",\n                        "generated_at": "2026-10-24T02:12:30+08:00",\n                        "platform_order_counts": {\n                          "taobao": 1200,\n                          "jd": 300\n                        },\n                        "platform_settle_commission_totals": {\n                          "taobao": 864000,\n                          "jd": 151000\n                        },\n                        "beneficiary_total_fen": 712000,\n                        "platform_retained_fen": 303000,\n                        "error_count": 4,\n                        "held_count": 2,\n                        "batch_count": 2,\n                        "draft_batch_count": 2,\n                        "created_at": "2026-10-24T02:00:00+08:00"\n                      },\n                      {\n                        "bill_id": "2026-08",\n                        "status": "settled",\n                        "generation_started_at": "2026-09-24T02:00:00+08:00",\n                        "generated_at": "2026-09-24T02:10:05+08:00",\n                    